= Geochemistry
{parent=Geology}

Study of the chemical composition and chemical processes of Earth materials.

= Geochemical discrimination diagram
{parent=Geochemistry}

A plot comparing chemical characteristics with reference fields for candidate origins. Overlap, alteration and nonunique petrogenesis limit direct inference of tectonic setting.

= Rare-earth element
{parent=Geochemistry}

A member of the rare-earth group used in source and melting studies through systematic differences in mineral-melt partitioning.

= Major element
{parent=Geochemistry}

An element present as a substantial component of a material, often reported for rocks through major-oxide abundances.

= Trace element
{parent=Geochemistry}

An element present at low abundance in a material; its partitioning can constrain sources and processes.

= Geochemist
{parent=Geochemistry}

= William M. White
{parent=Geochemist}
{c}

Author of <Geochemistry by William M. White>.

= Work by William M. White
{parent=William M. White}

